Japan in 60 Seconds · History in 60 Seconds series · Silkscreen Travel Poster style

Picture: drawn in code (Canvas 2D). Print engine engine/silk.js from the Lemo-Opuscar library (MIT).
Landmarks (raised-floor granary, five-storey pagoda, samurai helmet, castle keep, steam warship, ruined domed hall,
bullet train, lattice tower and city) are stylised silhouettes drawn as simple paths, not traced from photographs.
No logos, no brands, no maps or borders.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/):
  Big Shoulders Display — Patric King / Google Fonts
  Outfit — Rodrigo Fuenzalida / Google Fonts

Voice: Kokoro-82M v1.0 (hexgrad, Apache-2.0) via kokoro-onnx, voice bm_george. Checked with faster-whisper (MIT), model base.en.

Music (original score, music/compose.py): koto and shamisen by physical modelling (core/audio/pluck.py, Lemo-Opuscar, MIT);
taiko, shime-daiko and bamboo flute synthesised in code. No samples.
Sound (mix.py): squeegee, ink, screen, paper stamps, clips, wind, birds, sea, ship horn, train rush and city hum synthesised in code
(core/audio/sfx.py + mix.py).

Facts and sources: FACTS.md.
